PROPOSAL: product-direction decision for the maintainer; do not implement without a go-ahead.

Evidence: "\xEF\xBB\xBF# Title\nintro\n## Sub" gives a TOC with only "Sub", addressed "Sub" (should be "Title#Sub"); the intro is unaddressable (regex at Parser.pm:167).
Options: (a) strip a leading U+FEFF before parsing and keep it on write; (b) leave and document.
Recommendation: (a); it changes heading_paths on BOM pages only and belongs in the heading-recognition ADR.

2026-10-26 19:51 Decision (coordinator, on the maintainer's order to work the board off): option (a): strip a leading U+FEFF before parsing, keep it on write. Branch kopf.

Done in b6be2fd. Decision: the BOM is dropped by the parse only and stays in the page text, so writes keep it byte for byte without touching Document.
